>Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Shinsengumi was a special police force of masterless samurai formed in Kyoto in 1863 to protect the shogunate's representatives.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shinto"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shinto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shinto</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Shinto is the indigenous religion of Japan, centred on the worship of kami, spirits and deities present in nature, ancestors and places, at shrines served by priests.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shira-muren"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shira-muren.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shira Muren</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Shira Muren, or Xar Moron, is a river of eastern Inner Mongolia, China, the main upper source of the Liao River.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shirak"><span class="enc-name">Shirak</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Shirak is a historic district and modern province in north-western Armenia, a high plain along the Akhurian river around the city of Gyumri.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shiraz"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shiraz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shiraz</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Shiraz is a city in south-western Iran, known for its gardens and poets such as Hafez and Saadi.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shire-highlands"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shire-highlands.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shire Highlands</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Shire Highlands are an upland region of southern Malawi, east of the Shire River, around Blantyre and Zomba.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shirikti-shuqamuna"><span class="enc-name">Shirikti-Shuqamuna</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shirikti-Shuqamuna was king of Babylon for about three months around 985 BCE, the last ruler of the Bazi Dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shirkuh"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shirkuh.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shirkuh</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shirkuh was a Kurdish general in the service of the Zengid ruler Nur al-Din, and the uncle of Saladin.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shirley-baker"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shirley-baker.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shirley Baker</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shirley Baker was an English-born Wesleyan missionary who became adviser to George Tupou I of Tonga.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shiroishi-miyagi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shiroishi-miyagi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shiroishi, Miyagi</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Shiroishi is a city in southern Miyagi Prefecture, Japan, which grew around Shiroishi Castle, held under the Tokugawa by the Katakura family, senior retainers of the…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shirvanshah"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shirvanshah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shirvanshah</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Shirvanshah, &quot;king of Shirvan&quot;, was the title of the rulers of Shirvan in the eastern Caucasus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shishunaga"><span class="enc-name">Shishunaga</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shishunaga was a king of Magadha in eastern India and founder of the Shishunaga dynasty, which replaced the line of Bimbisara around the late 5th or early 4th century…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shishunaga-dynasty"><span class="enc-name">Shishunaga dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Shishunaga dynasty ruled the kingdom of Magadha in eastern India from around the late 5th century BCE until about 345 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shishuo-xinyu"><span class="enc-name">Shishuo Xinyu</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Shishuo Xinyu (A New Account of the Tales of the World) is a Chinese collection of anecdotes compiled about 430 under Liu Yiqing, a prince of the Liu Song dynasty.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shishupala"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shishupala.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shishupala</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shishupala is a king of Chedi in the Mahabharata, a cousin and enemy of Krishna.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shitthaung-temple"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shitthaung-temple.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shitthaung Temple</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Shitthaung Temple is a Buddhist temple at Mrauk U in Rakhine State, Myanmar, built by King Min Bin in 1535.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shiva"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shiva.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shiva</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Shiva is one of the principal gods of Hinduism, worshipped as the destroyer and transformer within the triad with Brahma and Vishnu, and as the supreme being by Shaivas.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shiva-simha-malla"><span class="enc-name">Shiva Simha Malla</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shiva Simha Malla was king of Kantipur (Kathmandu) in Nepal in the late 16th and early 17th centuries.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shivaji"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shivaji.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shivaji</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shivaji (1630–1680) was the founder of the Maratha state in western India and was crowned Chhatrapati in 1674.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shivaji-ii"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shivaji-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shivaji II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shivaji II was a Maratha ruler, son of Rajaram and Tarabai, proclaimed chhatrapati as a child in 1700 with his mother as regent.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shivaji-of-thanjavur"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shivaji-of-thanjavur.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shivaji of Thanjavur</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shivaji was the last Maratha raja of Thanjavur in southern India, son of Serfoji II, ruling from 1832 to 1855 with the administration already in British hands.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shivanasamudra"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shivanasamudra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shivanasamudra</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Shivanasamudra is an island town on the Kaveri River in Karnataka, India, beside waterfalls where the river drops from the Deccan plateau.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shivappa-nayaka"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shivappa-nayaka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shivappa Nayaka</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shivappa Nayaka was the greatest ruler of the Keladi Nayaka kingdom in coastal Karnataka, reigning from 1645 to 1660.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shivaskandavarman"><span class="enc-name">Shivaskandavarman</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Shivaskandavarman was one of the earliest known kings of the Pallava dynasty, ruling in the fourth century CE from Kanchipuram.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shivini"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shivini.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shivini</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Shivini was the sun god of Urartu, third in rank of the state pantheon after Haldi and the storm god Teisheba.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/shizhaishan"><span class="enc-name">Shizhaishan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Shizhaishan is a low hill near Jinning, by the southern shore of Lake Dian in Yunnan, China, site of a royal cemetery of the Dian kingdom.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/shkoder"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/shkoder.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Shkodër<